{
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse_num": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "I am the man that hath seen affliction by the rod of his wrath."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath led me, and brought me into darkness, but not into light."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Surely against me is he turned; he turneth his hand against me all the day."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "My flesh and my skin hath he made old; he hath broken my bones."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath builded against me, and compassed me with gall and travail."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath set me in dark places, as they that be dead of old."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath hedged me about, that I cannot get out: he hath made my chain heavy."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Also when I cry and shout, he shutteth out my prayer."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath inclosed my ways with hewn stone, he hath made my paths crooked."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He was unto me as a bear lying in wait, and as a lion in secret places."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath turned aside my ways, and pulled me in pieces: he hath made me desolate."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath bent his bow, and set me as a mark for the arrow."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath caused the arrows of his quiver to enter into my reins."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ arrows: Heb. sons"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 14,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "I was a derision to all my people; and their song all the day."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 15,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath filled me with bitterness, he hath made me drunken with wormwood."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ bitterness: Heb. bitternesses"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 16,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He hath also broken my teeth with gravel stones, he hath covered me with ashes."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ covered…: or, rolled me in the ashes"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 17,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "And thou hast removed my soul far off from peace: I forgat prosperity."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ prosperity: Heb. good"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 18,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "And I said,"
        },
        {
          "type": "speech",
          "speaker": "Unknown",
          "text": "My strength and my hope is perished from the LORD:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 19,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Remembering mine affliction and my misery, the wormwood and the gall."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ Remembering: or, Remember"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 20,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "My soul hath them still in remembrance, and is humbled in me."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ humbled: Heb. bowed"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 21,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "This I recall to my mind, therefore have I hope."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ recall…: Heb. make to return to my heart"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 22,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "¶ It is of the LORD’s mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": [
        "God's Mercies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 23,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 24,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "speech",
          "speaker": "My soul",
          "text": "The LORD is my portion,"
        },
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "saith my soul;"
        },
        {
          "type": "speech",
          "speaker": "My soul",
          "text": "therefore will I hope in him."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 25,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "The LORD is good unto them that wait for him, to the soul that seeketh him."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 26,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "It is good that a man should both hope and quietly wait for the salvation of the LORD."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 27,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "It is good for a man that he bear the yoke in his youth."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 28,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He sitteth alone and keepeth silence, because he hath borne it upon him."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 29,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He putteth his mouth in the dust; if so be there may be hope."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 30,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "He giveth his cheek to him that smiteth him: he is filled full with reproach."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 31,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "For the Lord will not cast off for ever:"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 32,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "But though he cause grief, yet will he have compassion according to the multitude of his mercies."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 33,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "For he doth not afflict willingly nor grieve the children of men."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ willingly: Heb. from his heart"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 34,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "To crush under his feet all the prisoners of the earth,"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 35,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "To turn aside the right of a man before the face of the most High,"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ the most High: or, a superior"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 36,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "To subvert a man in his cause, the Lord approveth not."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ approveth not: or, seeth not"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 37,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "¶ Who is he that saith, and it cometh to pass, when the Lord commandeth it not?"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": [
        "Divine Sovereignty"
      ]
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 38,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Out of the mouth of the most High proceedeth not evil and good?"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 39,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Wherefore doth a living man complain, a man for the punishment of his sins?"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ complain: or, murmur"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 40,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Let us search and try our ways, and turn again to the LORD."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 41,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Let us lift up our heart with our hands unto God in the heavens."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 42,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "speaker": "The people",
          "text": "We have transgressed and have rebelled: thou hast not pardoned."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 43,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou hast covered with anger, and persecuted us: thou hast slain, thou hast not pitied."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 44,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou hast covered thyself with a cloud, that our prayer should not pass through."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 45,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou hast made us as the offscouring and refuse in the midst of the people."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 46,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "All our enemies have opened their mouths against us."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 47,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Fear and a snare is come upon us, desolation and destruction."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 48,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Mine eye runneth down with rivers of water for the destruction of the daughter of my people."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 49,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Mine eye trickleth down, and ceaseth not, without any intermission,"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 50,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Till the LORD look down, and behold from heaven."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 51,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Mine eye affecteth mine heart because of all the daughters of my city."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ mine heart: Heb. my soul"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "text": "+ because…: or, more than all"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 52,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Mine enemies chased me sore, like a bird, without cause."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 53,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "They have cut off my life in the dungeon, and cast a stone upon me."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 54,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Waters flowed over mine head; then I said, I am cut off."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 55,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "¶ I called upon thy name, O LORD, out of the low dungeon."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": [
        "Prayer from Distress"
      ]
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 56,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou hast heard my voice:"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "speaker": "The LORD",
          "text": "hide not thine ear at my breathing, at my cry."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 57,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou drewest near in the day that I called upon thee:"
        },
        {
          "type": "divine",
          "speaker": "The LORD",
          "text": "thou saidst, Fear not."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 58,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "O Lord, thou hast pleaded the causes of my soul; thou hast redeemed my life."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 59,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "O LORD, thou hast seen my wrong: judge thou my cause."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 60,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou hast seen all their vengeance and all their imaginations against me."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 61,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Thou hast heard their reproach, O LORD, and all their imaginations against me;"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 62,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "The lips of those that rose up against me, and their device against me all the day."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 63,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Behold their sitting down, and their rising up; I am their musick."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 64,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "¶ Render unto them a recompence, O LORD, according to the work of their hands."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": [
        "Prayer for Justice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 65,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Give them sorrow of heart, thy curse unto them."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        [
          {
            "text": "+ sorrow…: or, obstinacy of heart"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    },
    {
      "verse_num": 66,
      "segments": [
        {
          "type": "hymnal",
          "text": "Persecute and destroy them in anger from under the heavens of the LORD."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "references": [],
      "heading": []
    }
  ]
}